course: dictionary
lesson: 419
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Approach is a good example. «The train is approaching the platform» means it is coming nearer. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Never approach a strange dog or a wild animal.» Here approach means go close to, and the clues strange and wild tell you to keep your distance. Try the swap: "Never come nearer to a strange dog" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The same word can be a noun too. «A new approach to fractions» means a way of doing a task, not a movement. Ask yourself: is it an action, or a way of solving a problem? Then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Ada wrote that her way of working was "poetical science", so an approach can also mean a method of thinking. Ask what the writer is trying to do. The answer tells you which meaning to use.
fact: To approach something means to come nearer to it.
fact: To approach someone means to go to them to speak or ask for something, like «approach a teacher for help».
fact: An approach is a way of dealing with a problem, like «a different approach».
fact: An approach is also a path or road leading to a place.
fact: Phrases to know: «approach with care», «the approach of winter», «approaching fast».
exercise: «The train is approaching the platform.» What does approaching mean here? | Leaving quickly | Stopping for ever | *Coming nearer | Painting it
exercise: «Approach a teacher for help if you are stuck.» What does approach mean? | *Go to and ask | Give away | Run away from | Hide under
exercise: Mia tries a new approach to fractions. What is the approach here? | A small wooden bridge | A type of fraction | *A way of solving the problem | A loud noise
test: «Approach a horse from the side, near its shoulder, and talk softly as you come.» What does approach mean here? | Look at it from far off | Feed it quickly | *Move towards it carefully | Ride away on it
test: What does approach mean in «the approach of winter»? | A path to a house | *The coming of winter, getting nearer | Leaving the country | A way to solve sums
exam: What does approach mean in «The approach to the village was muddy»? | Going to ask for help | *A road leading to a place | A way of solving a sum | Coming nearer to someone
